  ('315ef358-6786-55fb-a7ce-2b460db8a8b8', 'Public Relations and Advertising', 'Administration', 'B.Sc/B.A', '["explain the different meanings of communication", "highlight the various elements of the communication process", "distinguish between different types of human communication and their features", "explain the roles of communication; and", "outline the different forms of African traditional forms of communication", "outline the constituents of modern communication forms", "explain the changing delivery forms in modern communication", "compare and contrast between national media systems in the modern world; and", "discuss the challenges posed to national media systems by globalization", "define the concept of public relations", "identify the composition of the environment of public relations in Nigeria", "analyse the Public Relations Environment in Nigeria; and", "appreciate the public relations career/business prospects and challenges in the Nigerian environment. Course Description — Public relations as a discipline and profession operates within any particular environment, otherwise called the internal and external environments of public relations. This course therefore introduces the student to the context of Public Relations in Nigeria. It briefly defines concepts of public relations and environmental scanning. It introduces the student to the historical, political, geographical, economic, legal, socio-cultural, religious and technological contexts of public relations in Nigeria. It exposes the various tools for analysing the contexts of public relations in the Nigerian environment. Other topics include understanding the nature of Nigeria''s democracy; legal systems; demography; free enterprise economy; ethnic and religious compositions of Nigeria; technological, and physical environmental contexts as they impact public relations discipline and practice in Nigeria. The career and business prospects in the fascinating field of public relations are also discussed. ---", "how PR originated", "the stages of the development of PR in America", "the origin of PR in Nigeria", "the present state of PR practices in Nigeria", "the challenges facing PR practices in Nigeria; and", "the key historical leaders in PR evolution both in America and Nigeria", "highlight the origin and development of media in Nigeria", "explain the factor that have influenced the development of the media; and", "outline the roles the media have played in Nigeria''s development", "analyse the different definitions of PR, the Mexican statement, British and American institutes of PR and other scholarly definitions", "have a smart knowledge of the evolution of PR globally and Nigeria", "comprehend the relationship between PR and related disciplines", "identify the channels or media of public relations", "distinguish the differences between PR and other PR tools like marketing and advertising; and", "analyse the basic principles of PR practice", "examine the role of Public Relations in integrated marketing communications", "develop simple campaign plan", "explain the role of Public Relations in a free market economy; and", "outline the four-step public relations process", "appreciate the necessity for cordial relations between organizations and media", "recognize the processes involved in building good media relations between organizations and practitioners", "identify the consequences of poor media relations on the organisation", "identify the various media, their characteristics, needs and demands; and", "discuss the uses of the media by PR practitioners to meet their communicational and organizational needs", "have good knowledge of the language of visual imagery – have ability to develop a blog in class as a tool to interact with his/her wider audience", "have a good understanding of how to build an integrated campaign and website, using such software like: Photoshop, in design, dream weave, flash and other applications", "have understanding of the process of design which includes: ideation, strategy, and execution; and", "have a fair grip of the dynamics of social media and its usage in PR; be knowledgeable of such social media platforms like: Facebook, Twitter, LinkedIn and YouTube and how to employ them in Public Relations practice", "comprehend how to write press releases", "identify feature articles projecting the image of the organization", "explain rejoinders to negative publicity; and", "describe how to produce educational literature like diary, calendar, annual reports, coverage brochure", "explain the relationship between PR and other sectors of the economy and the society at all levels, CSOs and commercial organization; and", "explain how PR functions in commercial organizations such as banks, insurance companies etc and how they differ from PR in non-profit-organization", "identify all the PR tools that are essential for success of the economy, politics and society", "have a good grasp of marketing communication and its impact on the environment and society", "explain the place of PR in prospective minority groups interest; and", "discuss the criticisms of PR", "identify the relationship between PR and Advertising i.e., similarities and differences", "recognise the elements of promotion and how it can be used in produce or service campaigns for the benefit of the sponsors; and", "discuss the concept of integrated marketing communication (IMC)", "explain the dynamics of PR in a diverse setting", "explain the application of PR to promote national integration and unity", "discuss the use of PR in managing shocks and conflicts in a multicultural setting; and", "explain use of PR in promoting international social relations", "identify, explain and compare theoretical concepts", "apply theories to real communication and media situations", "critique theories, pointing out their strengths and limitations; and", "explain and apply any of the theories in research and practice. ---", "explain the meaning and features of scientific research", "distinguish between scientific research and other ways of knowing", "discuss the various types of research methods", "explain the practical applications of conducting research", "outline the process of conducting research", "explain sampling procedure, population, sample; and", "explain the importance of ethics in media and communication research", "distinguish between qualitative and quantitative data", "outline the different ways of presenting research data", "apply different software for data analysis; and", "discuss how to draw inferences, from data and significance of research findings", "define research", "appreciate the importance of research in PR", "identify the types of PR research e.g., effectiveness survey, image survey, trends survey, motivation survey, content analysis etc.; and", "comprehend the meaning and application of the term RACE: Research, Action, Communication and Evaluation as applied to PR cases or problems", "demonstrate both theoretical/practical understanding of the key issues needed to develop strong global brands", "analyse cases to understand past successes and failures in strategy and why; and", "demonstrate depth knowledge of total culture in communication and emerging issues in brand globalisation", "explain key components of a brand''s identity and how they work in creating brand equity", "outline factors that shape success or failure of a proposed strategic direction", "analyse how cultural differences can impact on brands; and", "construct, through collaborative work, a brand promotion task", "define what is meant by CSR", "identify the Schools of thought in CSR", "explain corporate social investments, patronage, donations etc.; and", "explain how corporate organisations can use CSR to leverage their reputation, brand personality", "recognize the dynamics of financial PR e.g., financial news analysis, AGM: what it is and how it is organized", "capital market, banking relationship, investors relations