  ('826d263c-6052-567a-b845-ee74ceea58c3', 'International Studies and', 'Arts and Humanities', 'B.A', '["identify the ancient ancestors of the contemporary international systems", "list the chain of events and monumental changes that culminated in the emergence of the contemporary international system", "trace and link the collapse of ancient political system in Europe, Asia, and Africa to the emergence of the contemporary international political system", "analyse the structure of the contemporary international system; and", "provide examples of miniature political arrangements put in place for peaceful co-existence among different political units before the emergence of the contemporary international system", "explain how the fragmentation of powerful ancient empires, notably the roman empire and the byzantine empires paved way for the evolution of contemporary international system", "analyse how the treaty of Westphalia in 1648 and the defeat of napoleon in 1815 facilitated the evolution of the contemporary international system", "state how the industrial revolution changed the structure of the world economy and created capitalism and later imperialism", "explain the diffusion of power among different states and non-state actors as a consequence of the evolution of contemporary international system", "discuss the shift in the balance of regional and global powers", "explain the emergence of new centres of power; and", "state the increasing importance of regional integration and the rise of interdependence and globalization", "explain African liberation from the shackles of colonialism", "state the nature of politics in post-colonial Africa", "discuss the establishment of the organization of African unity (OAU) to rid Africa of all colonial vestiges", "explain the politics of succession to power and retention of power after independence", "discuss the incidence of direct military intervention in African politics", "analyse the establishment of the African Union (AU