g: a. design of machine components; b. product design and innovation; c. part modelling and drafting in solidworks; and d. technical report writing. 400 Level GET 402 Engineering Project I (2 Units C: PH 90) Learning Outcomes", "describe the construction and operating principles of food and beverage processing plants, handling and packaging systems using engineering terminologies", "design food processing plants, and undertake feasibility studies", "explain boilers, water supply and waste disposal systems", "discuss types, causes and preventive measures of industrial accidents; and", "apply first aid measures to industrial accident victims", "identify the major grains and state their processing principles and utilisation", "discuss the importance of grains in daily diet", "describe the nutritional value of different grains", "state the milling processes and develop practical skills in determining the composition of grains", "elaborate the complete flour making process and use of cereals in different product manufacturing", "explain storage needs of grains, microflora and contaminants; and", "manage stored grains", "describe the science and technology underpinning the composition and manufacturing of beer", "explain brewing technology and beer production", "acquire detailed theoretical understanding of the role of the raw ingredients of beer production on beer quality; and", "discuss the operations of malting, mashing and hop chemistry", "operate food processing equipment, exploring the differentr types available", "describe mechanical processes involving compression, shear or impact force", "discuss unit operations: Description; Sorting: Operates similarly to and overlaps with grading; and", "explain the process of cleaning and remove foreign matter and contamination", "account for the most common methods used for consumer-targeted sensory evaluations", "explain how sensory evaluation and the human sensory physiology can be used as tools in product development", "co