ent should be introduced to the concept of product/component design and innovation and then be given a comprehensive design project. Examples of projects should include the following: a. design of machine components; b. product design and innovation; c. part modelling and drafting in solidworks; and d. technical report writing. 400 Level GET 402 Engineering Project I (2 Units C: PH 90) Learning Outcomes", "demonstrate the knowledge of the mathematical concepts applied in biomedical engineering, including linear relations and functions, systems of inequalities", "apply the best mathematical method for addressing a particular bioengineering problem", "formulate bioengineering problems in terms of appropriate mathematical modelling methods", "analyse biological data using appropriate mathematical methods", "evaluate the output of the mathematical modelling methods concerning the underlying biological processes", "manipulate experimental data using mathematical methods; and", "assess the output of the mathematical analysis of a bioengineering problem", "apply knowledge and awareness of the basic principles and concepts of biology, computer science, and mathematics", "design, deploy and use the various electronic health information systems", "simulate biomedical systems experimentation and design with the aid of computer systems", "explore the massive biological data available and their manipulation with the computer systems", "utilise existing software effectively to extract information from large databases and to use this information in computer modeling; and", "develop problem-solving skills, including the ability to develop new algorithms and analysis methods", "apprehend the general principle and practice of biotechnology", "explain the structure and function of cell organelles and cellular transport", "describe the science of biotechnology and identify its product domains", "comprehend the concepts in human genetics and its applications", "identify the various natu