  ('ccf8d2ee-f184-5994-937a-7be43999cf5f', '980bbe04-8ef6-5eab-a60f-ef76f3203594', '827725e6-f5aa-5689-9903-55f3fedbc137', NULL),
  ('2c35bd66-905b-5706-9d82-4153a1465d01', 'e7c6659e-a0dc-560a-943f-4ec52c0df473', 'c86f37a2-3e51-57e2-81ec-a20ff1550352', NULL),
  ('74034502-67fb-5f6f-85d5-ad1eed9ec608', '26ce26b0-5eac-5286-b8b5-179e56a6b320', 'c86f37a2-3e51-57e2-81ec-a20ff1550352', 'DE: requires very good passes in three JUPEB/A'' Level subjects â€” Theatre Arts: Literature in English and any two of Igbo/Yoruba, CRS/IRS, French, History, Government, Music and Visual Arts; Visual Arts: Visual Arts and any two of Igbo/Yoruba, CRS/IRS, French, History, Government and Music; Music: Music and any two from Literature in English, Igbo/Yoruba, CRS/IRS, French, History, Government, Economics, Chemistry, Biology, Further Mathematics and Visual Arts. Also accepts HND/OND at Upper Credit Level in Drama/Theatre and Music; NCE Music and Diploma or Advanced level in Music from the Royal School of Music London, Trinity College London and Musical Society of Nigeria (MUSON). O''Level: (a) Theatre Arts â€” Five O/Level credit passes in English Language, Literature-in-English, Mathematics and any other two subjects one of which must be an Arts subject; (b) Music â€” Five O/Level credit passes in English Language, Mathematics, two Arts subjects (may include Music) and any other subject; (c) Visual Arts â€” Five O/Level credit passes in English Language, Mathematics, two Arts subjects (may include any one of Fine Arts/Visual Arts/Photography/Craft Practice/Dyeing & Bleaching/Painting & Decoration) and any other subject. UTME subjects: accepts English Language, any one of Fine Arts/Literature-in-English/Music, one Arts subject and any Science or Social Science.'),
  ('1e4aea10-2d2d-5682-9d58-fb633a408a15', '7aeec5b4-cf56-5d90-bfa4-3371a6f54bb9', 'c86f37a2-3e51-57e2-81ec-a20ff1550352', 'DE: accepts A/level passes in GCE or HSC or IJMB or JUPEB in two (2) Art subjects including Literature in English, in addition to UTME entry requirements in two (2) Arts subjects including English Language, with an overall merit level Pass from a recognized College of Education. O''Level: requires Five (5) O Level Credits in English Language and any other four (4) subjects from Literature in English, History/Government, CRK/IRK, Economics, Mathematics, Biology, Chemistry, Agricultural Science, Physics, Igbo/Hausa/Yoruba, Fine Art, Geography, Commerce. UTME subjects: requires any other three (3) subjects from the same list.'),
  ('35d36af0-e1c1-58a4-8ed0-3a2a7f00c02e', 'f90909a4-fcc6-5899-a1a5-dd43ce3cbbc8', 'c86f37a2-3e51-57e2-81ec-a20ff1550352', 'DE: (a) three (3) GCE ''A'' Level passes in Fine Arts or Technical Drawing plus the UTME requirements; (b) HND holders with an average of B grade with the UTME requirements into 300 level; (c) ND credit or NCE merit with the UTME requirements; (d) candidates would be interviewed. O''Level: requires five (5) ''O'' Level credit passes to include English Language, Fine and Applied Arts and one Science subject; candidates with NBC/NTC must have five (5) ''O'' Level credit passes including English language, Technical drawing, Painting and Decorating and a Science subject.'),
  ('fa8f531e-2d39-53ff-9566-db23904ea5a7', '88ceb89a-3f4c-583f-88da-2a5691321979', 'c86f37a2-3e51-57e2-81ec-a20ff1550352', NULL),
  ('22c1598b-6698-57d9-bbdb-bfd7bc9116d2', '4da5b3d4-5a61-5de1-88ae-859b326f069e', 'c86f37a2-3e51-57e2-81ec-a20ff1550352', NULL),
  ('d554c409-1af4-579a-b7e4-be493dac66c5', '4208cf5b-56b9-56ab-809d-9d17f1f3488d', 'c86f37a2-3e51-57e2-81ec-a20ff1550352', NULL),
  ('0c74eef5-86b8-5042-8c39-8383e54363ec', 'f421bff4-b271-55b8-a090-5e0227d3618d', 'c86f37a2-3e51-57e2-81ec-a20ff1550352', NULL),
  ('73d00a1e-6c96-58fe-bca0-940cd8de32db', '7f1e09fa-66eb-50d0-b12b-a66eecc30366', 'c86f37a2-3e51-57e2-81ec-a20ff1550352', 'DE: in addition to the UTME requirements, candidates must have any of the following â€” OND in Fine Arts/Industrial Arts at Lower Credit level / HND / NCE: Fine Arts at Merit Level; IJMB minimum of 9 points. O''Level: requires Five (5) credit passes at SSCE, GCE, NECO and NABTEB O'' Level including English Language, Mathematics and three other relevant subjects in not more than two sittings; credit level pass in Fine Arts/Visual Arts is an added advantage.')
