  ('53c139a2-c439-593c-bdbc-319fb96b4d8e', 'e1c071b0-e046-51f0-9de7-77ac53886688', 'bb3a4631-728f-5640-83f6-63247ecfd460', 'DIRECT ENTRY: IBADAN accepts two (2) `A'' Level passes to include Yoruba and another Arts or Social Science subject. It accepts NCE credit/merit in Yoruba and another Arts or Social Science subject. | UTME: IBADAN requires five (5) `O'' Level credit passes at one sitting or six (6) `O'' Level credit passes at two (2) sittings including English Language and two (2) Arts subjects, one of which must be Yoruba. | UTME SUBJECTS: IBADAN requires Yoruba and two (2) other subjects in Arts or Social Sciences.'),
  ('d45edebe-d0a2-5d57-8cb9-ce0f1706c9db', 'be4981eb-2b54-5ea1-941d-44e8ca2774db', 'bb3a4631-728f-5640-83f6-63247ecfd460', 'DIRECT ENTRY: ILORIN requires a) At least two (2) `A'' Level passes to include Yoruba and any other Arts/Social Science; b) NCE/Diploma (Upper Credit) in Yoruba and Social Science subject. | UTME: ILORIN accepts five (5) `O'' Level credit passes to include Yoruba, English Language, Mathematics and two (2) other Arts/Social Science subjects. It also accepts candidates who do not offer Yoruba (Language/Literature) but meet other UTME entry requirements. | UTME SUBJECTS: ILORIN requires Yoruba and two (2) other subjects in Arts/Social Science.'),
