  ('179c2cd1-aa07-5e20-b4d7-52bceb9d197f', '8ad8b817-0045-5081-8f1d-af80ae4f1e41', '649cf22c-50a0-5328-8ce4-19c582fb9616', NULL),
  ('e5efa6ea-8c6b-5bac-889d-331ef821f2fc', 'e7c6659e-a0dc-560a-943f-4ec52c0df473', '649cf22c-50a0-5328-8ce4-19c582fb9616', NULL),
  ('0fd9599f-c76d-590f-aa98-d85bc7936c4f', 'd3a418de-b72b-5553-b672-82cfbccacf14', '649cf22c-50a0-5328-8ce4-19c582fb9616', NULL),
  ('3e519607-e907-5c23-80af-fc90c228e5ae', 'f3bd8dbc-ffcb-5d4b-8e8d-310ce5ef5f55', '649cf22c-50a0-5328-8ce4-19c582fb9616', 'Accepts a) first degree in relevant programmes and HND upper credit into 400 level of the five-year programme; b) ND lower credit; c) for Quantity Surveying ''A'' Level/ND upper credit in Building and Quantity Surveying; d) for Surveying and Geoinformatics, two ''A'' level passes in Mathematics and Physics plus UTME requirements, accepts ND/HND in Land Surveying and Geoinformatics from Federal School of Surveying or other NBTE accredited institution; e) ''A'' Level Cambridge; f) ND upper credit into 200 level from Federal School of Surveying or other NBTE accredited institution. | UTME: for Surveying and Geoinformatics, ''O'' Level credit passes in English Language, Mathematics, Physics and any two from Chemistry, Geography, Biology, Technical Drawing, Fine and Applied Arts and Economics; also requires five ''O'' Level credit passes to include Mathematics, Physics, English Language and any other science subject; accepts either Physics or Chemistry. | UTME SUBJECTS: for Surveying and Geoinformatics, Mathematics, Physics and any one from Chemistry, Geography, Economics, Government, Biology or Agricultural Science.'),
  ('114f1294-3f75-5be8-a5b7-7b804e2cf92d', '4b767c85-a5d3-5578-b266-246db57463f3', '649cf22c-50a0-5328-8ce4-19c582fb9616', NULL),
  ('7b8bccd0-58f7-525e-904a-7efb8ec7139e', '6fefc7fb-cd39-503b-8899-4aacfbd2c30e', '649cf22c-50a0-5328-8ce4-19c582fb9616', NULL),
  ('6c030613-e974-5979-b8c3-89234c2570cd', 'cd4edfad-172a-5f76-b45e-f806306ef788', '649cf22c-50a0-5328-8ce4-19c582fb9616', NULL),
  ('6e41a17f-6830-5e35-85ad-ea72bd3dd972', '2a117a94-b271-5351-a623-6616184fe452', '649cf22c-50a0-5328-8ce4-19c582fb9616', 'Accepts a) ''A'' Level passes at Credit level (CIE/IJMB/JUPEB) or equivalent in at least two of Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry, Geography and Economics; b) ND at Upper Credit level in Quantity Surveying or Building Technology or other relevant fields in Environmental Design and Management. For Surveying and Geoinformatics: a) ND in Surveying and Geoinformatics or related field with minimum Upper credit from NBTE-accredited programme; b) GCE or equivalent with minimum credit in at least two subjects including Mathematics and Physics. | UTME: requires five (5) SSC credit passes at maximum two sittings in English Language, Mathematics, Physics and any two of Chemistry, Economics, Building Construction, Technical Drawing, Geography, Government. For Surveying and Geoinformatics, five SSC credit passes in Mathematics, Physics, English Language and any two of Geography, Elementary Surveying, Technical Drawing, Chemistry, Economics, Fine Art, Biology/Agricultural Science. | UTME SUBJECTS: Mathematics and Physics plus one subject from Chemistry, Building Construction, Technical Drawing, Geography, Economics and Government. For Surveying and Geoinformatics, Mathematics, Physics and either Chemistry or Geography.'),
  ('101b1540-67bb-5bba-9de5-967bc2967ee7', '05eb9c1c-cd59-53b8-9e55-bf415b7ba4f5', '649cf22c-50a0-5328-8ce4-19c582fb9616', NULL),
  ('24e4198c-65fc-5284-8d71-55a8b0975494', 'a9560228-6453-5527-8eb6-9f5c346fabb0', '649cf22c-50a0-5328-8ce4-19c582fb9616', 'Requires a) at least three ''A'' Level passes not below C in Mathematics, Physics and Chemistry; b) ND/HND at Upper Credit in Physics, Mathematics, Statistics, Computer Science, Geology, Environmental Sciences or Engineering; c) First Degree in same fields; d) very good passes in three JUPEB subjects (Mathematics, Physics and Chemistry). Does not accept NCE; candidates must also meet ''O'' Level requirements. Same requirements apply for Quantity Surveying. | UTME: requires at least five ''O'' Level credit passes in English Language, Mathematics, Chemistry, Physics and any one of Fine Arts, Technical Drawing, Geography, Economics and Biology in not more than two sittings. For Quantity Surveying, at least five ''O'' Level credit passes in English Language, Mathematics, Chemistry, Physics and any other science subject in not more than two sittings; at least a Pass required in Biology. | UTME SUBJECTS: Physics, Chemistry and Mathematics.'),
  ('af7d5004-b15e-5ce0-9c23-1196560d7989', 'f3d31093-b900-5185-a4ef-b3dbb37cb373', '649cf22c-50a0-5328-8ce4-19c582fb9616', NULL),
