  ('df88f1a8-7838-5bb9-809f-c58f29e2b71a', 'be4981eb-2b54-5ea1-941d-44e8ca2774db', '649cf22c-50a0-5328-8ce4-19c582fb9616', 'Accepts a) Advanced level, H.S.C/IJMB or equivalent passes in Mathematics and Physics or any of Geography, Technical Drawing, Economics, Chemistry, Commerce, Building Construction and Biology into 200 level; b) OND certificate in Quantity Surveying, Building, Architecture and allied professions at upper credit level into 200 level; c) HND in Quantity Surveying with Upper credits in both ND and HND into 300 level. | UTME: requires five (5) SSCE credits in English Language, Mathematics, Physics and any other subjects from Geography, Technical Drawing, Economics, Chemistry, Commerce, Building Construction and Biology. | UTME SUBJECTS: Mathematics, Physics and any one of Geography, Technical Drawing, Economics, Chemistry.'),
  ('21a2c8ea-4999-51f3-b4c9-084111596d2b', '308b7f5a-13c7-5fc0-8c29-5cac2ac5d469', '649cf22c-50a0-5328-8ce4-19c582fb9616', 'No Direct Entry; accepts ND credit in Land Surveying and ''A'' Level passes in Mathematics and Physics plus UTME requirements into 200 level; ''O'' Level credit pass in Geography an advantage. | UTME: accepts Mathematics and any other subject. | UTME SUBJECTS: Mathematics, Physics and Geography.'),
